T3c · stage 1a · 2026-09-13 · commit dc1f47e — the Punish deadline, the xmrswap command line as two processes
============================================================================================================
Plan: docs/MAINNET_TEST_PLAN.md §6 T3c, "Stage 1" (T1's command-line pair on the simulator, against an htlc a simhtlc
run installed, Monero on regtest). Machine paths are written <repo>, <tmp>, <user>. No key, password or channel key is
in this file; the channel key was made with `xmrswap channel-key` and passed through XMRSWAP_CHANNEL_KEY only.

Build: xmrswap built with go1.26.8 at dc1f47e (sha256 ad8504d5…). At dc1f47e -prover takes
`wsl.exe -e <path inside WSL>` and pins the WSL binary itself, so no wrapper and no -prover-sha256 were used.

The commands (a scratch harness started them, killed them and restarted them; bob and alice were separate processes):
  bob:   xmrswap bob   -state <tmp>/cli/t3c/bob.json   -dero 127.0.0.1:30006 -monero http://127.0.0.1:28084 -monero-name <bob's wallet>
                       -t1 48 -t2 16 <common>
  alice: xmrswap alice -state <tmp>/cli/t3c/alice.json -dero 127.0.0.1:30007 -monero http://127.0.0.1:28083 -monero-name <alice's wallet>
                       -claim-margin 8 <common>
  common: -net regtest -daemon 127.0.0.1:20000 -htlc bfc9da5a387e945515b741480ed1df1cf8550db018e7cab16b1658bd3322dbb3
          -monerod 127.0.0.1:28081 -prover "wsl.exe -e <path to the pinned proof-xmr build>" -amount-dero 2000
          -amount-xmr 1000000000000 -t1-min 10 -t2-min 6 -gate-deadline 4 -g2-min 30 -channel <tmp>/cli/t3c/channel
  The plan's flags, with the htlc the dc1f47e simhtlc run installed (w1min 10, w2min 6, g2 30). Every other flag at its
  default (confs 0 = the tier's 20, stable 8). The Monero wallets s1cli-1789225277-alice (funded by mining 4 regtest
  blocks to it) and s1cli-1789225277-bob, made for these runs; the harness mined one regtest block about every 6 s.
  "Stop" was a hard kill (taskkill /F): a console Ctrl-C cannot be sent from the harness. The companion saves every
  step durably, so a hard stop is the harsher of the two.

What happened (the driver log below has every line with its DERO height)
  16:52:46  both started. bob locked (lock 4, 9cf4ff65…, block 3412; t1 3459, t2 3475) and paid the stipend (block 3422).
  16:56:45  T3b step 1: bob killed in watching_xmr (h 3423).
  17:06:27  T3b step 2: alice, after her Monero lock (d5568e77…), reached await_refund at h 3455, before t2 3475, and was
            killed there. Her punish cutoff t2 + g2 − (11 + 8 + 8) = 3478; t2 + g2 = 3505.
  17:13:22  T3c step 2: alice restarted at h 3478, her cutoff. Her log: "height 3478 is past the punish cutoff 3478
            (t2 3475 + g2 30 − 11 validity − 8 stable − 8 margin): not punishing; waiting for bob's Reclaim",
            punish_window -> await_reclaim. punishTx empty in her state.
  17:13:50  a second kill of alice in await_reclaim and an immediate restart (a T9 row, folded in): the restart was
            refused by the companion, "alice.json.lock was touched 12s ago: another companion is running on this
            state" (see the note below). Alice stayed stopped from here to 17:35.
  17:21:35  T3c step 3, h 3505 = t2 + g2, lock 4 open (st_4 0): Punish sent by hand from wallet 30018. In the plan's form
            (curl without a Content-Type header) the wallet RPC answered HTTP 415 with an empty body and sent nothing;
            with -H 'Content-Type: application/json' it sent 33758ff3…. Mined in block 3506 and refused: st_4 still 0
            at h 3508. 30018 paid its 3,000 fee and nothing else moved.
  17:22:21  T3c step 4 (T3b's step 3, here past t2 + g2): bob restarted at 3508. "height 3509 is at or past the refund
            cutoff 3464 (t2 3475 − 11) with the lock open: no Refund is sent", refund_window -> punish_window ->
            reclaiming; his Reclaim 4fce032b… went out and was mined in block 3510.
  17:22:50  bob killed 2 s into reclaiming (a T9 row, folded in), after the Reclaim had been sent; his immediate
            restart was refused the same way ("bob.json.lock was touched 14s ago").
  17:35:08  both started again by hand with the same commands and the same channel key, once the dead processes' lock
            files were stale. bob: reclaiming -> reclaim_confirming -> reclaimed (stable at 3551), with no second
            Reclaim; alice (T3b step 4): st_4 4 -> refund_seen -> sweep_ready -> sweeping -> swept, her XMR back
            (eab3c9b2…).

Note on the refused restarts. xmrswap takes a lock file beside the state (XMR-04) and refuses to start while it was
touched recently ("another companion is running on this state"). A process killed hard leaves its lock file as fresh as
a live one's, so a restart made at once is refused until the file ages. That is the guard working (a second copy must
be refused, §6 T9), and it was the harness's error to restart at once. The plan's T9 wording, "kill the process hard …
then run the same command again", should add: once the dead process's lock file is stale.

